# FROZEN shared contracts — content hashes.
#
# CLAUDE.md: amending a contract is a deliberate, announced change. This file is the
# mechanism. tests/contracts/frozen.test.mjs recomputes each sha256 and fails
# if it moved, so a change that edits a schema to fit its own code is caught at
# merge instead of at runtime by whichever consumer assumed the other shape.
#
# CHANGING A CONTRACT IS A DELIBERATE, ANNOUNCED ACT:
#   1. propose the change to the other consumers (it is a shared contract)
#   2. edit _lib/contracts/<name>.schema.json
#   3. update the hash below IN THE SAME COMMIT, with the reason in the message
#   4. re-run:  node --test 'tests/**/*.test.mjs'
#
# Recompute with:  shasum -a 256 _lib/contracts/*.schema.json
#
# Frozen at: 2026-08-28.
#
# AMENDED 2026-08-28, applying the change requests the consumers
# filed instead of editing the schemas themselves (the procedure worked):
#   api-catalog  + pricing.page_gated      (cost runtime: `bounded` and "needs page-gating"
#                                           are different predicates; two consumers each
#                                           computed 11 endpoints and got different sets)
#   journal-line + dry_run, list_key, an `error` short-code pattern, attempt minimum 0
#                                          (journal: a planned row must be distinguishable
#                                           from a row killed mid-call, and a free-text
#                                           error is the easiest PII leak into a journal)
#   ledger-line  + estimate_basis, row_id, hop, and a `known_zero` cost_status
#                                          (cost runtime: an estimate is the only number for 11
#                                           endpoints, so its basis must be legible;
#                                           journal: a ledger line could not join to a
#                                           journal unit, so per-row cost audit was impossible)
#
# AMENDED 2026-08-30, authorised by the merge owner:
#   api-catalog  field_map_status + "keys_from_spec_example"
#                                          (catalog: the generator now publishes
#                                           `field_map_keys` — the top-level key NAMES of
#                                           the spec's 200 example, corroborated
#                                           byte-identical against the backend's generated
#                                           richapi-endpoints.manifest.json output_schema.
#                                           `field_map` itself stays null, so law 2 is
#                                           intact: this is a key list, not a mapping, and
#                                           it is a DIFFERENT TYPE (array, not object) so
#                                           no consumer can confuse the two. The old
#                                           two-value enum forced every such row to claim
#                                           TODO_no_usable_example, which was a lie in the
#                                           other direction.)
#
# AMENDED 2026-09-17, description text only, authorised by the repository owner:
#   api-catalog, journal-line, ledger-line: internal planning references removed from
#   `description` and `$comment` strings before the public release. No type, enum,
#   `required` or pattern changed.

# AMENDED 2026-09-17, on live-run evidence:
#   ledger-line  + billed, not_billed_reason, credits_estimated_if_billed
#                                          (cost runtime: the ledger booked the
#                                           would-have-been price of calls the API never
#                                           billed. Measured on the 2026-09-17
#                                           local-business-outbound rerun: 27 lines summing
#                                           41.5 credits in `credits_estimated`, of which 14
#                                           non-2xx lines carried 28.0 — while the receipt
#                                           for the same run correctly reported those as
#                                           free. /measure, /cost-optimizer and every budget
#                                           gate sum the LEDGER, so a run could be stopped by
#                                           a ceiling it had not approached. `credits_estimated`
#                                           is now 0 on an unbilled line and the estimate moves
#                                           to `credits_estimated_if_billed`, a name nothing
#                                           sums by accident. `billed`/`not_billed_reason` make
#                                           the second unbilled case legible: a 2xx whose body
#                                           says `billed: false` because the provider errored —
#                                           recorded live from email_finder, and NOT a not-found.)

